1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,050
This is InTune: an AI interpreter between
people who communicate differently.

2
00:00:05,665 --> 00:00:07,110
Say it your way. Be understood.

3
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:08,565
And plan together.

4
00:00:09,191 --> 00:00:11,841
We’re Coding Claws, at HackGT 13.

5
00:00:12,471 --> 00:00:16,579
Nagur Shareef Shaik, Sahith Reddy
Thummala, Pranav Nagothu, and Geethanjali

6
00:00:16,659 --> 00:00:17,721
Nagaboina.

7
00:00:18,425 --> 00:00:20,570
This project started with a friend.

8
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:24,375
I grew up with a close friend who found
conversations hard.

9
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:29,158
In groups, he struggled to keep up, and I
often watched him get lost in the

10
00:00:29,238 --> 00:00:30,663
conversation.

11
00:00:31,344 --> 00:00:34,719
I always wished I could build something to
help him.

12
00:00:35,391 --> 00:00:37,773
Today, AI makes that possible.

13
00:00:37,853 --> 00:00:42,923
So I built InTune, so that nobody has to
feel lost in a group, and no friend has to

14
00:00:43,003 --> 00:00:44,416
watch it happen.

15
00:00:45,024 --> 00:00:49,532
He wasn’t alone. Autistic adults are far
more likely to feel lonely, and it’s

16
00:00:49,612 --> 00:00:51,999
rarely for lack of wanting to connect.

17
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:56,675
Research shows where it breaks: when
autistic and non-autistic people pass on a

18
00:00:56,755 --> 00:01:00,005
story, details get lost, and rapport
drops.

19
00:01:00,589 --> 00:01:04,839
It’s called the double empathy problem,
because the gap runs both ways.

20
00:01:05,508 --> 00:01:08,608
So InTune doesn’t ask anyone to change how
they talk.

21
00:01:09,218 --> 00:01:13,968
Instead, AI interprets in both directions,
inside small, private circles.

22
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:18,736
Meet Maya. These are her chats: circles of
friends and family, and one-to-one

23
00:01:18,816 --> 00:01:20,116
conversations.

24
00:01:20,726 --> 00:01:25,171
She can share a status, like “replies may
be slow”, so nobody has to explain a quiet

25
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:26,251
day.

26
00:01:26,691 --> 00:01:31,311
And messages carry tone tags, like “just
asking” or “no rush”, so meaning isn’t

27
00:01:31,391 --> 00:01:32,791
left to guesswork.

28
00:01:33,391 --> 00:01:37,449
Here’s a message from Maya’s sister: “It’d
be nice if you could maybe bring something

29
00:01:37,529 --> 00:01:38,529
small?”

30
00:01:39,047 --> 00:01:41,530
Is that a question? Does she need to
reply?

31
00:01:41,610 --> 00:01:45,972
Maya has translation switched on, so
InTune explains it right underneath.

32
00:01:46,575 --> 00:01:50,883
In plain words, it shows what’ s being
asked, that a reply is expected, and

33
00:01:50,963 --> 00:01:52,450
what’s still unclear.

34
00:01:53,073 --> 00:01:56,598
Only Maya sees this, and her sister’s
words never change.

35
00:01:57,275 --> 00:02:01,832
Now the other direction. Leo is autistic
too, and when talking is hard, he writes

36
00:02:01,912 --> 00:02:03,175
in shorthand.

37
00:02:03,767 --> 00:02:08,367
He taps Translate, and InTune turns it
into clear words that keep his meaning.

38
00:02:08,992 --> 00:02:12,742
Leo sees exactly what his friends will
read, and who will read it.

39
00:02:13,325 --> 00:02:16,095
He adds a tone, “not upset”, and approves
it.

40
00:02:16,175 --> 00:02:18,800
The AI can never send anything by itself.

41
00:02:19,388 --> 00:02:23,633
It’s labelled as AI-assisted and approved
by Leo, and a built-in check flags any

42
00:02:23,713 --> 00:02:26,438
“not”, time or name that goes missing.

43
00:02:27,083 --> 00:02:29,678
InTune also learns each person’s own
words.

44
00:02:29,758 --> 00:02:32,833
When talking gets too much, Leo says “red
light”.

45
00:02:33,408 --> 00:02:37,228
He saved what that means in his
phrasebook, so InTune uses his meaning,

46
00:02:37,308 --> 00:02:38,433
not a guess.

47
00:02:39,066 --> 00:02:42,248
Maya will read that he’s overwhelmed and
needs to stop for now.

48
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:44,266
Leo approves, and it’s sent.

49
00:02:44,891 --> 00:02:48,536
On the other side, Maya understands
straight away, and she can see Leo

50
00:02:48,616 --> 00:02:50,641
approved those exact words.

51
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:52,900
She replies in her own words.

52
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:55,717
Messages like this never need AI at all.

53
00:02:56,325 --> 00:03:00,520
People can share how they like to be
spoken to, on a “How to talk with me” card

54
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,300
that their circles can see.

55
00:03:02,893 --> 00:03:06,563
They keep a phrasebook of their own
expressions, like “loud box”, meaning

56
00:03:06,643 --> 00:03:08,193
“it’s too noisy here”.

57
00:03:08,788 --> 00:03:12,188
And they can choose calm colours that are
easy on the senses.

58
00:03:13,116 --> 00:03:15,061
Circles stay small and private.

59
00:03:15,141 --> 00:03:18,641
People join only by invitation, right
inside the app.

60
00:03:19,226 --> 00:03:22,696
Before joining, you see exactly who will
read your posts, so there are no

61
00:03:22,776 --> 00:03:23,901
surprises.

62
00:03:24,548 --> 00:03:26,123
One tap, and you’re in.

63
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:28,707
Group chats are where people get lost.

64
00:03:28,787 --> 00:03:31,775
Here, Maya’s friends are trying to plan a
weekend.

65
00:03:32,406 --> 00:03:34,763
Sunday, not Saturday. Somewhere quiet.

66
00:03:34,843 --> 00:03:38,831
Mornings are better. And Jordan needs an
exact start and end time.

67
00:03:39,426 --> 00:03:41,551
Priya taps “Plan it together”.

68
00:03:42,794 --> 00:03:47,064
InTune reads the chat, and what each
person shared about how they communicate,

69
00:03:47,144 --> 00:03:50,044
and drafts one plan that everyone can
enjoy.

70
00:03:50,632 --> 00:03:54,827
It shows how the plan works for each
person, like a quiet place for Maya and a

71
00:03:54,907 --> 00:03:56,532
morning start for Leo.

72
00:03:57,154 --> 00:04:00,604
Anything still open becomes a simple,
direct question.

73
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:04,449
Priya checks the exact text, and posts it
to the group.

74
00:04:05,383 --> 00:04:09,728
Calls can be the hardest part, so InTune
brings a calm, live interpreter into the

75
00:04:09,808 --> 00:04:10,808
call.

76
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:15,562
Leo joins. The screen stays steady:
nothing jumps around, and a soft ring

77
00:04:15,642 --> 00:04:17,055
shows who’s talking.

78
00:04:17,629 --> 00:04:22,161
When Leo speaks, everyone gets captions,
and Maya’s private interpreter explains

79
00:04:22,241 --> 00:04:24,104
each line in plain words.

80
00:04:24,699 --> 00:04:29,199
If Leo needs a moment, one tap sends a
signal, without interrupting anyone.

81
00:04:29,777 --> 00:04:32,384
And when speaking is hard, he can type
instead.

82
00:04:32,464 --> 00:04:37,552
InTune suggests clear words, he approves
them, and everyone hears them read aloud.

83
00:04:38,144 --> 00:04:40,819
When the call ends, nothing from it is
kept.

84
00:04:43,350 --> 00:04:45,895
So why not just use WhatsApp with Meta AI?

85
00:04:45,975 --> 00:04:49,570
It’s great for everyday chat, and its
assistant can help you write.

86
00:04:49,650 --> 00:04:54,050
InTune also interprets the other way, so
you understand what others mean.

87
00:04:54,655 --> 00:04:58,050
A person always approves the exact words
and who sees them.

88
00:04:58,130 --> 00:05:03,630
The AI never sends on anyone’s behalf, and
a lost “not”, time or name is flagged.

89
00:05:04,222 --> 00:05:08,479
And it’s built around each person: their
own phrases, how they like to be spoken

90
00:05:08,559 --> 00:05:11,997
to, and plans and calls that fit
everyone’s needs.

91
00:05:12,616 --> 00:05:15,186
Throughout, AI helps, and people decide.

92
00:05:15,266 --> 00:05:19,341
It never quietly drops a fact, and it
never guesses anyone’s feelings.

93
00:05:19,925 --> 00:05:25,258
And if the AI is down, everyone can still
talk: messages, phrases, calls, blocking

94
00:05:25,338 --> 00:05:27,425
and reporting all work without it.

95
00:05:28,025 --> 00:05:30,720
Privacy is built in, not bolted on.

96
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:35,974
Circles are invitation-only, reading help
is private, and calls are never recorded.

97
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:40,842
Voice and video clips are deleted once
they’re turned into words, InTune never

98
00:05:40,922 --> 00:05:45,460
asks for a diagnosis, and anyone can
delete their account at any time.

99
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:50,337
It’s designed around data-protection
principles, like data minimisation and the

100
00:05:50,417 --> 00:05:51,929
right to erasure.

101
00:05:52,583 --> 00:05:57,183
InTune brings people closer, without
asking anyone to become someone else.

102
00:05:57,757 --> 00:06:02,107
It’s live today. Try it with the demo
accounts, and read the code on GitHub.

103
00:06:02,717 --> 00:06:05,742
From all of us at Coding Claws, thank you
for watching.
